    "created_at": "2022-11-14T16:08:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-14T16:08:03Z",
    "body": "I think having this implemented as class methods is preferable as it will need operator-type specific handling unless we only want to (e.g.) support `SpinOp` labels without exponents. Also the handling in the case of `VibrationalOp` will need special care as I would expect this to permute modes and not their modals.\r\n\r\nSo I would go with your second suggestion: `op.permute_indices(...)`. I agree that the ordering can be done the same way as `np.transpose` does it.\r\n\r\nSince this is again a comparatively small feature, I will rename the issue to reflect that any `SparseLabelOp` subclass should support this in order to ensure feature parity.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
